{# ── 2. Why teach AI? ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
<section class="teacher-why">
  <div class="teacher-why-inner">
    <h2 class="teacher-why-heading">Why teach AI?</h2>
    <p class="teacher-why-text">AI tools are not magic. They are systems designed by people that make mistakes and carry the values of their designers. Students who understand how these systems work can question, challenge and build them themselves.</p>
    <div class="teacher-why-principles" role="list">
      <div class="teacher-why-principle" role="listitem">Learning by doing – including about AI systems.</div>
      <div class="teacher-why-principle" role="listitem">Using one's own data makes data meaningful.</div>
      <div class="teacher-why-principle" role="listitem">AI can be understood without knowing how to code.</div>
      <div class="teacher-why-principle" role="listitem">Learning is best done together.</div>
      <div class="teacher-why-principle" role="listitem">Teaching must be grounded in research.</div>
      <div class="teacher-why-principle" role="listitem">Design is based on children's rights.</div>
    </div>
    <a class="teacher-why-cta" href="https://gen-ai.fi/fi/materials/basics" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read AI Fundamentals for Teachers <span class="teacher-step-lang-note">(in Finnish)</span> →</a>
  </div>
</section>

